WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.468
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.503 --> 00:06.771
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:06.806 --> 00:10.341
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.377 --> 00:13.344
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.380 --> 00:16.848
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.883 --> 00:20.151
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.187 --> 00:21.719
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.755 --> 00:23.087
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.123 --> 00:24.323
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.933 --> 00:36.100
<i>Today's
feature presentation of Glory</i>

00:36.135 --> 00:37.468
will not be seen.

00:37.503 --> 00:39.770
What? Aw, I love that movie.

00:39.806 --> 00:42.206
Aw, man, that's gonna leave
a big hole in their lineup.

00:42.241 --> 00:43.774
<i>What's gonna fill
the Glory hole?</i>

00:43.810 --> 00:45.910
<i>In place of Glory,
we will be showing Shaft,</i>

00:45.945 --> 00:47.411
starring Richard Roundtree.

00:47.447 --> 00:49.647
<i>What? You can't just shove
Shaft in the Glory hole.</i>

00:49.682 --> 00:51.549
Yeah, I know. It'd
be better to put in

00:51.584 --> 00:53.451
that movie about the two
girls who meet Nixon.

00:53.486 --> 00:54.919
<i>What's that movie
called? Dick?</i>

00:54.954 --> 00:56.554
<i>Dick would slide right
into that Glory hole.</i>

00:56.589 --> 00:58.255
<i>No, no, Dick's too short
for that Glory hole.</i>

00:58.291 --> 01:01.258
<i>But if you also put in
Edward Furlong's movie, Pecker,</i>

01:01.294 --> 01:03.227
<i>you got Pecker and Dick
in the Glory hole,</i>

01:03.262 --> 01:05.696
and you got a tight squeeze,
but it-it ought to fit.

01:06.733 --> 01:08.466
The hell am I sitting on?

01:08.501 --> 01:10.434
Oh, hey, that's
my old rope toy.

01:10.470 --> 01:11.969
I was wondering
where that was.

01:12.004 --> 01:14.004
Ew, what would you want
that for? It's gross.

01:14.040 --> 01:15.172
No, it's not.
It's awesome.

01:15.208 --> 01:16.741
I can suck on it
for the flavor.

01:16.776 --> 01:19.043
I can thrash it around,
pretend it's a snake.

01:19.078 --> 01:20.711
Sometimes I just
bite it like this.

01:20.747 --> 01:22.379
Rope!

01:22.415 --> 01:24.315
That's stupid.

01:24.350 --> 01:25.516
I want it.

01:25.551 --> 01:26.984
Well, you can't
have it; it's mine.

01:27.019 --> 01:28.619
Oh, yeah?
Not for long it ain't.

01:30.990 --> 01:32.656
Come on, Brian,
I need this rope

01:32.692 --> 01:37.161
in case I open
a nautical-themed restaurant.

01:37.196 --> 01:38.996
We got boat parts on the wall,

01:39.031 --> 01:41.565
so you know the crab
comes from the ocean.

01:41.601 --> 01:45.002
Eating next to a porthole!
What?!

02:01.821 --> 02:03.701
No, no, no, no, I don't
want to make that trade.

02:03.723 --> 02:05.156
I thought I wanted
to make that trade,

02:05.191 --> 02:10.161
but I don't want to
make that trade.

02:10.196 --> 02:12.596
Hey, Chris.
Where's your father?

02:12.632 --> 02:15.332
He's still trying to get
that rope away from Brian.

02:15.368 --> 02:17.434
He's got to give up
that obsession.

02:17.470 --> 02:19.336
I don't like what
it's doing to him.

02:19.372 --> 02:20.671
Precious.

02:20.706 --> 02:22.840
Wants precious rope.

02:22.875 --> 02:24.742
Peter, enough with
the rope.

02:24.777 --> 02:27.178
Also wants ice cream.

02:27.213 --> 02:29.480
No, Peter, it's too close
to dinnertime.

02:29.515 --> 02:32.116
Get ice cream anyway.

02:32.151 --> 02:34.118
Don't you dare.

02:34.153 --> 02:36.220
All right,
but I'll be back in a moment

02:36.255 --> 02:38.823
as another movie thing.

02:38.858 --> 02:40.858
I am Johnny Five.

02:40.893 --> 02:42.359
Need input.

02:42.395 --> 02:44.328
Input is ice cream.

02:44.363 --> 02:46.931
I need ice cream.

02:46.966 --> 02:49.300
Did I say I'm
Johnny Five yet?

02:49.335 --> 02:52.570
You didn't go
to work today, did you?

02:56.943 --> 02:59.510
So, still got
that rope, I see.

02:59.545 --> 03:01.145
Well, I got a
better rope.

03:01.180 --> 03:02.680
That's not a chewing rope.

03:02.715 --> 03:04.415
I know. It's a tying rope!

03:14.827 --> 03:16.794
Come on, Brian,
you'd better let go.

03:16.829 --> 03:18.863
I told you this is mine!
You're never gonna get it!

03:24.170 --> 03:26.737
Just give me the rope.
Nobody has to get hurt, Brian.

03:28.774 --> 03:31.075
Only one person has
to get hurt, Brian.

03:58.804 --> 04:01.105
My teeth!

04:01.140 --> 04:03.274
Oh! Oh, man!

04:03.309 --> 04:05.242
I'm real sorry about
your mouth, Brian.

04:05.278 --> 04:07.244
Damn it, Peter.
What were you thinking?

04:07.280 --> 04:09.747
This has to be the stupidest
thing you've ever done.

04:09.782 --> 04:11.682
No, Brian. The stupidest
thing I ever did

04:11.717 --> 04:14.118
was turn the bubbles
off in a hot tub.

04:14.153 --> 04:16.153
Yeah! Party!

04:18.157 --> 04:20.991
Ew, bath with friends.

04:25.498 --> 04:27.298
Now, remember, Brian's probably

04:27.333 --> 04:29.199
very self-conscious
about how he looks,

04:29.235 --> 04:31.201
so let's try to be supportive.

04:31.237 --> 04:33.037
Brian! Dinner!

04:36.042 --> 04:37.808
So, everybody, how was your day?

04:37.843 --> 04:39.977
What's for dinner?
I'm starving.

04:41.180 --> 04:43.781
My God, you look like
one of those animals.

04:43.816 --> 04:45.215
You know, the
one that...

04:45.251 --> 04:47.718
Which one does the
sound?

04:47.753 --> 04:50.054
That... Aw, crap, you
know which one I mean.

04:50.089 --> 04:51.956
Oh, who am I kidding?

04:51.991 --> 04:54.658
You got to take me to the
dentist to get my mouth fixed.

04:54.694 --> 04:57.561
Brian, we can try to make you
feel a little less repulsive,

04:57.596 --> 04:59.396
but we're not spending

04:59.432 --> 05:01.298
human money on a
deformed animal.

05:01.334 --> 05:04.001
What? Then what am I
supposed to do?

05:04.036 --> 05:06.670
I don't know. But here,
you can have this back.

05:06.706 --> 05:09.006
It's boring.
It doesn't do anything.

05:09.041 --> 05:11.608
You know what?
Go to hell, Peter!

05:12.778 --> 05:15.145
Wow, this is
the craziest meal I've had

05:15.181 --> 05:17.982
since I had lunch
at Tommy Sullivan's house.

05:18.017 --> 05:21.018
Very good macaroni and
cheese, Mrs. Sullivan.

05:21.053 --> 05:22.820
Thank you, Chris.

05:22.855 --> 05:24.688
That was just
awful, Chris.

05:24.724 --> 05:25.724
Terrible.

05:25.725 --> 05:27.224
He is not ready
for flashbacks.

05:27.259 --> 05:29.259
No, he is not.

05:34.033 --> 05:35.499
Hey, listen,

05:35.534 --> 05:37.668
thanks for not laying into
me like everybody else.

05:37.703 --> 05:39.770
I don't care enough about you
to lay into you.

05:39.805 --> 05:41.038
But now that you mention it,

05:41.073 --> 05:42.906
your face looks like
a used condom.

05:42.942 --> 05:45.175
Yeah, I know.

05:48.381 --> 05:49.513
Oh, come on, Brian.

05:49.548 --> 05:50.714
Don't do that.

05:50.750 --> 05:52.249
Don't cry. Be a man.

05:52.284 --> 05:53.550
I'm not crying!

05:53.586 --> 05:56.086
Look, listen, just...
here, just take this.

05:56.122 --> 05:57.254
What is this?

05:57.289 --> 05:58.422
That's my dentist.

05:58.457 --> 06:00.090
He'll bill me.
I've got an account.

06:00.126 --> 06:01.892
You've got an account
with a dentist?

06:01.927 --> 06:04.561
He sells me nitrous
at wholesale, I bang his wife.

06:04.597 --> 06:06.964
Those both sound
like things for you.

06:06.999 --> 06:09.600
Look, you want
his number or not?

06:09.635 --> 06:12.770
I won't forget this,
Glenn Quagmire.

06:12.805 --> 06:14.905
Don't ever say my name
like that, okay?

06:14.940 --> 06:16.540
And don't tell anybody
about this.

06:16.575 --> 06:19.777
Now get the hell out of the bar,
you pathetic son of a bitch.

06:19.812 --> 06:22.846
Hey, language.
My big fat black mom is here.

06:22.882 --> 06:25.883
I know I didn't just hear
what that man said.

06:25.918 --> 06:28.485
Jerome, you got to go
to extra church!

06:28.521 --> 06:31.121
Aw, Mom.

06:34.660 --> 06:38.462
<i>We now return to
My Dinner with Andre the Giant.</i>

06:38.497 --> 06:40.597
I could never give up
my electric blanket;

06:40.633 --> 06:42.199
it's cold in New York City.

06:42.234 --> 06:44.568
You may argue that this is
a waste of energy,

06:44.603 --> 06:47.638
but to me, it's worth the
comfort because, let's face it,

06:47.673 --> 06:50.174
the world is
an abrasive place.

06:50.209 --> 06:54.144
I have maybe hours to live,
and you're wasting them.

06:54.180 --> 06:56.146
Hey, I'm, uh...

06:56.182 --> 06:57.915
I'm back from getting
my new teeth.

06:57.950 --> 07:00.317
Well, come on in, Brian.
Let's see them.

07:00.352 --> 07:02.352
All right, here it goes.

07:05.891 --> 07:08.492
Oh, my God!
Look at your teeth!

07:08.527 --> 07:11.061
Hey, maybe you could
help us build the dam.

07:11.097 --> 07:13.330
If you think you got
the chops for it.

07:13.365 --> 07:14.731
Well, think about it.

07:14.767 --> 07:17.000
It's something to chew on.

07:18.104 --> 07:20.104
We use him
just the right amount.

07:23.923 --> 07:26.357
So be honest, huh?
You guys hate them.

07:26.392 --> 07:28.225
No, Brian, are you kidding?

07:28.261 --> 07:30.828
They're spectacular!
You look like a movie star.

07:30.863 --> 07:32.129
Really?

07:32.165 --> 07:35.199
Yeah, you're like an even
more handsome Adam Carolla.

07:35.234 --> 07:37.268
God, I can't believe
you guys really like them.

07:37.303 --> 07:41.105
Yeah, Brian, you are gonna
get so much sweet tail!

07:41.140 --> 07:43.040
Oo-cha, oo-cha,
oo-cha, oo-cha!

07:43.075 --> 07:44.975
Brian, you have
found your look.

07:45.011 --> 07:47.244
That is the best cosmetic
surgery in this family

07:47.280 --> 07:48.979
since Lois got
her boob job.

07:49.015 --> 07:50.247
I don't know
what happened.

07:50.283 --> 07:52.149
I told the
doctor C-cups.

07:52.185 --> 07:53.617
I told him something else.

07:53.653 --> 07:56.187
I think he did
a dam good job.

07:56.222 --> 07:58.656
Okay, now we've used him
too much.

08:03.663 --> 08:04.995
♪ When you're smiling ♪

08:05.998 --> 08:09.667
♪ When you're smiling ♪

08:09.702 --> 08:14.805
♪ The whole world
smiles with you ♪

08:14.841 --> 08:17.141
♪ When you're laughing ♪

08:18.177 --> 08:21.345
♪ When you're laughing ♪

08:21.380 --> 08:26.250
♪ The sun comes
shining through ♪

08:26.285 --> 08:29.420
♪ But when you're crying ♪

08:29.455 --> 08:31.822
♪ You bring on the rain ♪

08:31.858 --> 08:34.425
♪ So stop your sighing ♪

08:34.460 --> 08:37.094
♪ Be happy again ♪

08:37.129 --> 08:39.997
♪ Keep on smiling ♪

08:40.032 --> 08:43.267
♪ 'Cause when you're smiling ♪

08:43.302 --> 08:49.974
♪ The whole world
smiles with you. ♪

08:52.578 --> 08:54.378
Oh, good, you're
already here.

08:54.413 --> 08:55.413
I'm sorry?

08:55.414 --> 08:57.248
Can we ask you a few questions?

08:57.283 --> 08:58.916
Uh... yeah, sure.

08:58.951 --> 09:00.417
Is this a good
neighborhood?

09:00.453 --> 09:01.952
Uh, yeah,
it's a great neighborhood.

09:01.988 --> 09:04.121
Lot of families,
good parks.

09:04.156 --> 09:06.824
Uh, six fire hydrants,
but they are unavailable.

09:06.859 --> 09:08.525
They are previously claimed.

09:08.561 --> 09:10.160
They belong to some badass.

09:10.196 --> 09:12.830
Okay, but do you think
this house will hold its value?

09:12.865 --> 09:14.131
I don't see why not.

09:14.166 --> 09:15.499
It's got a nice porch.

09:15.534 --> 09:17.635
And the yard's got
plenty of room for little ones.

09:17.670 --> 09:20.537
Although that's really
up to the two of you.

09:22.008 --> 09:24.408
Hey, so sorry I'm late.
Let me show you the house.

09:24.443 --> 09:27.878
No need to. Your partner
already sold us on it.

09:27.914 --> 09:29.413
Sorry, I-I
didn't realize

09:29.448 --> 09:31.215
they thought I was
a real estate agent.

09:31.250 --> 09:34.051
You are a real estate agent;
you just don't know it yet.

09:34.086 --> 09:34.985
What do you mean?

09:35.021 --> 09:36.021
Look at that smile.

09:36.022 --> 09:37.855
You're a born salesman.

09:39.225 --> 09:40.891
You should
come work for me.

09:40.927 --> 09:43.294
Huh. Never thought
I'd be in real estate.

09:43.329 --> 09:44.828
You think I
can handle it?

09:44.864 --> 09:47.665
Every other divorced mom
at my kid's school is a realtor.

09:47.700 --> 09:49.867
I think you can handle it.

09:55.975 --> 09:58.676
Bonnie, I still don't get why
you want to see this house.

09:58.711 --> 10:00.244
The foundation is
totally out of whack.

10:00.279 --> 10:02.012
I mean, the-the whole
house is slanting down

10:02.048 --> 10:03.280
to that cliff
over there.

10:03.316 --> 10:07.084
Uh-huh. Can you open
the sliding door?

10:14.427 --> 10:16.593
I'll take it.

10:18.631 --> 10:20.064
So tell me again,
where's the lake?

10:20.099 --> 10:21.099
Right there.

10:21.100 --> 10:22.399
And where's the
summer camp?

10:22.435 --> 10:23.435
Right over there.

10:23.436 --> 10:24.436
I'll take it.

10:24.437 --> 10:26.270
Now, I am obligated
to disclose

10:26.305 --> 10:28.472
that the previous owners
were murdered in this house.

10:28.507 --> 10:29.573
Whoa, buddy!

10:29.608 --> 10:31.875
Quit drilling; you
already struck oil.

10:33.879 --> 10:36.580
I just don't know if this
is the right time to buy.

10:36.615 --> 10:37.881
Yeah, you're probably right.

10:37.917 --> 10:39.883
Maybe we should wait
till you graduate college.

10:39.919 --> 10:42.753
Thank you, but I'm
actually 42 years old.

10:42.788 --> 10:45.122
Uh, that's not credible.

10:46.792 --> 10:49.126
Hello, Doctor?
I need a new pair of eyes

10:49.161 --> 10:51.295
because clearly
mine aren't seeing straight.

10:52.865 --> 10:55.733
You know what?
Maybe I am ready to buy.

10:55.768 --> 10:57.201
Great! I'll get the paperwork.

10:57.236 --> 10:58.902
Hello? Hello?

10:58.938 --> 11:00.337
What's going on with your eyes?

11:00.373 --> 11:01.572
Oh, uh, nothing.
Everything's fine.

11:01.607 --> 11:03.540
Is this the guy
who wanted his pulse checked

11:03.576 --> 11:05.109
because he died
and went to heaven?

11:05.144 --> 11:06.243
Uh, yes.

11:06.278 --> 11:07.444
Please stop calling.

11:07.480 --> 11:10.080
This is a very busy
doctor's office.

11:10.116 --> 11:12.449
♪ Where you from ♪

11:12.485 --> 11:13.951
♪ You sexy thing ♪

11:13.986 --> 11:15.719
♪ Sexy thing, you. ♪

11:19.525 --> 11:22.760
Brian, five sales this week.
You're killing it.

11:22.795 --> 11:25.362
Yeah. And last night,
I closed another big deal.

11:25.398 --> 11:26.530
Kim in marketing.

11:26.565 --> 11:28.332
What are the specs?

11:28.367 --> 11:30.467
She's a two breast,
one ass fixer-upper.

11:30.503 --> 11:32.703
The entire property was
covered in a thick brush.

11:33.906 --> 11:37.374
Everyone in the office
besides us is garbage.

11:37.410 --> 11:38.909
Wow, Brian, you're
doing great here.

11:38.944 --> 11:40.210
You're really on fire.

11:40.246 --> 11:42.880
Thanks. I guess I should
stop, drop, and roll.

11:42.915 --> 11:43.915
Whoa.

11:43.949 --> 11:45.416
That's enough.

11:45.451 --> 11:48.085
The only thing is, anyone
can sell a nice house,

11:48.120 --> 11:51.088
but a real star is someone
who can sell a dump.

11:51.123 --> 11:52.589
I can sell anything.

11:52.625 --> 11:55.092
Well, we got this crap
condo down by the marina.

11:55.127 --> 11:57.261
We haven't been able to
unload it in two years.

11:57.296 --> 12:00.431
You find some sucker to buy
it, and I'll make you partner.

12:00.466 --> 12:01.832
All right, sounds good.

12:01.867 --> 12:02.966
It's a plan.

12:03.002 --> 12:04.768
Hey, did I tell you about
Kim in marketing?

12:04.804 --> 12:05.936
You mean my wife Kim?

12:05.971 --> 12:08.038
I'm gonna go sell
that condo.

12:12.411 --> 12:15.012
God, there's got to be a sucker
to buy this condo.

12:15.047 --> 12:16.647
Guys, this is on me.

12:16.682 --> 12:19.216
I just hit 20 years in the air,
and I got a big bonus.

12:19.251 --> 12:21.919
It's sad
when planes 'splode.

12:21.954 --> 12:22.954
What?

12:22.988 --> 12:23.988
Yeah, I guess.

12:23.989 --> 12:25.389
Anyway, I am flush.

12:25.424 --> 12:27.958
For the first time in my life,
I got money to burn.

12:30.996 --> 12:33.697
Looks like I found my sucker.

12:52.799 --> 12:54.532
Whoa. What?

12:54.567 --> 12:56.701
I didn't know you worked out
at this gym, too.

12:56.736 --> 12:58.870
Hey, Brian. Hang on,
I'm just finishing a set.

12:58.905 --> 12:59.937
Come on, come on, two more.

12:59.973 --> 13:01.973
Come on, come on,
you got to want it.

13:07.547 --> 13:08.547
Nice job.

13:08.548 --> 13:10.281
Let's get you a rubdown.

13:10.316 --> 13:11.916
I'm glad I bumped into you
because I've been meaning

13:11.951 --> 13:13.284
to give you something.

13:13.319 --> 13:14.319
What's this?

13:14.320 --> 13:16.053
That is the money you loaned me.

13:16.089 --> 13:18.456
Oh. That's pretty cool. Thanks.

13:18.491 --> 13:19.657
You're welcome.

13:19.692 --> 13:21.826
I just wish I could do
something more for you.

13:21.861 --> 13:24.195
Hmm, I could make you rich.

13:24.230 --> 13:25.563
No, no, no, that's just money.

13:25.598 --> 13:26.797
I'll think of something else.

13:26.833 --> 13:27.865
What're you talking
about, Brian?

13:27.901 --> 13:29.333
No, no, no, I've said too much.

13:29.369 --> 13:31.449
The one thing they're pretty
firm about at the office

13:31.471 --> 13:33.271
is you don't take
the inside deals

13:33.306 --> 13:35.039
and give them to your friends.

13:35.074 --> 13:37.642
What... What kind of inside
deal are you talking about?

13:38.678 --> 13:40.011
All I can say is...

13:40.046 --> 13:42.213
underpriced waterfront property

13:42.248 --> 13:44.849
that's guaranteed
to appreciate in value.

13:44.884 --> 13:46.117
That's all I can say.

13:46.152 --> 13:48.586
Oh, wait, a-are you bothered
by sorority noise, though?

13:48.621 --> 13:49.987
I-I don't know, Brian.

13:50.023 --> 13:51.756
I don't know if I'm a
real estate investor.

13:51.791 --> 13:53.357
Well, you might
surprise yourself.

13:53.393 --> 13:56.160
I mean, I didn't think I'd ever
be friends with Ice-T.

13:58.031 --> 13:59.263
What are you
thinkin' about?

13:59.299 --> 14:02.033
Thinking about putting
black guy hair in a ponytail.

14:02.068 --> 14:05.069
'Cause the times change,
but I don't.

14:08.408 --> 14:09.941
All right, guys,
here it is.

14:09.976 --> 14:11.509
Prescott Towers.

14:11.544 --> 14:15.046
Quahog's premier luxury
living experience.

14:18.117 --> 14:22.253
Nestled somewhere between the
ocean and your imagination:

14:22.288 --> 14:23.821
<i>Prescott Towers.</i>

14:23.856 --> 14:26.123
<i>Quahog's only luxury residence</i>

14:26.159 --> 14:29.193
<i>catering exclusively
to the affluent.</i>

14:29.229 --> 14:31.062
<i>Affluent means rich.</i>

14:31.097 --> 14:32.964
<i>Come live in the kind of place</i>

14:32.999 --> 14:36.133
<i>a Persian guy would say
is a little much.</i>

14:38.771 --> 14:40.638
The ceiling is a pool.
The ceiling is a pool.

14:40.673 --> 14:42.139
Quagmire, you got to get this.

14:42.175 --> 14:44.475
I don't know about buying
a place without seeing it first.

14:44.510 --> 14:46.310
Of course not. I
wouldn't expect you to.

14:46.346 --> 14:48.579
But as your friend, I wanted
to let you know early

14:48.615 --> 14:50.881
because there's another buyer
who's about to snap it up.

14:50.917 --> 14:52.617
I think he's a
pilot for Delta.

14:52.652 --> 14:53.751
Delta?

14:53.786 --> 14:55.219
It's not Lew Sheridan,
is it?

14:55.255 --> 14:57.154
Well, I'm not really
permitted to say.

14:57.190 --> 14:58.356
Do you like
Lew Sheridan?

14:58.391 --> 14:59.557
I hate Lew Sheridan.

14:59.592 --> 15:01.626
It's Lew Sheridan.
That son of a bitch!

15:01.661 --> 15:03.794
Say what you want, but he's got
an eye for real estate. Let me

15:03.830 --> 15:05.930
just give him a call and let him
know he's gonna get the place.

15:05.965 --> 15:07.932
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

15:07.967 --> 15:09.300
Okay. I'll take it.

15:09.335 --> 15:11.235
All right. You
won't be sorry.

15:11.271 --> 15:13.070
Yeah, that condo
looks awesome.

15:13.106 --> 15:15.006
You're makin'
a smart move, Quagmire.

15:15.041 --> 15:17.808
Like I did when I wanted to
get out of that boring meeting.

15:17.844 --> 15:19.910
Third quarter projections
indicate our sales

15:19.946 --> 15:21.812
will be down 40%.

15:21.848 --> 15:23.781
Why don't we go through
the profit-loss statement

15:23.816 --> 15:25.950
line by line from
the past six quarters,

15:25.985 --> 15:28.486
which will offer us a good
cost analysis comparison

15:28.521 --> 15:30.421
that I think we'll
be able to utilize

15:30.456 --> 15:32.923
as we move forward - Aah!
into the next fiscal year.

15:32.959 --> 15:34.425
Hey, guys,
I got to leave.

15:34.460 --> 15:36.994
I got a nosebleed,
and, uh, I don't work here.

15:41.834 --> 15:43.701
All right, Quagmire,
now when you introduce us

15:43.736 --> 15:45.036
to the ladies
by the pool,

15:45.071 --> 15:47.004
I'm a millionaire,
Joe's a war hero,

15:47.040 --> 15:48.873
and Cleveland
is Magic Johnson.

15:48.908 --> 15:50.608
I own a lot
of theaters.

15:50.643 --> 15:53.544
I hope you don't know
much else about me.

15:58.418 --> 15:59.550
Is this the right address?

15:59.585 --> 16:00.785
This doesn't look
like the building

16:00.820 --> 16:01.986
from Brian's presentation.

16:02.021 --> 16:03.187
Come on, Quagmire.

16:03.222 --> 16:05.056
Never judge a book
by its cover.

16:05.091 --> 16:06.457
Or a movie.

16:07.927 --> 16:09.694
No.

16:17.437 --> 16:20.037
It's probably nothing,
but there's a stain on the rug

16:20.073 --> 16:21.472
in the shape of a little kid.

16:21.507 --> 16:23.107
I don't know if
you want this now,

16:23.142 --> 16:25.643
but I bought you
a mini cactus.

16:25.678 --> 16:27.945
What the hell?
This is a dump.

16:27.980 --> 16:30.614
Well, maybe it's still
got a nice ocean view.

16:30.650 --> 16:33.484
The harbor is poisoned.

16:33.519 --> 16:35.286
Damn it.
Brian screwed me.

16:35.321 --> 16:37.922
That's why I've never made any
major investments with my dog.

16:37.957 --> 16:39.190
What am I gonna do?

16:39.225 --> 16:41.559
I sank my entire bonus
into this place.

16:41.594 --> 16:43.394
Let me see your
contract, Quagmire.

16:43.429 --> 16:45.396
There's got to be
a way out of this.

16:45.431 --> 16:47.531
I'm gonna kill him,
that's what I'm gonna do.

16:47.567 --> 16:49.133
ClubAmigos.

16:49.168 --> 16:50.868
That's what we're gonna
call this place.

16:50.903 --> 16:54.138
Here it is. You've got
72 hours after closing

16:54.173 --> 16:56.774
to rescind the
purchase. State law.

16:56.809 --> 16:59.710
Thank God. I got to go
tell Brian the deal's off.

16:59.746 --> 17:02.012
Oh, there's a head
in the freezer.

17:02.048 --> 17:04.181
Ooh, and sherbert.

17:07.286 --> 17:08.853
We're looking for
Brian Griffin.

17:08.888 --> 17:10.521
I'm still within 72 hours,
and I want

17:10.556 --> 17:11.822
to get out of my contract.

17:11.858 --> 17:14.125
You'd have to speak to
Mr. Griffin about that.

17:14.160 --> 17:16.127
But I'm sorry, he's
not in the office.

17:16.162 --> 17:17.328
Where the hell is he?

17:17.363 --> 17:18.529
Slow down, Quagmire.

17:18.564 --> 17:20.164
This sounds like
a discussion to have

17:20.199 --> 17:22.199
over a cone-shaped cup of water.

17:25.171 --> 17:26.437
Ah.

17:26.472 --> 17:28.939
You can drink from these
and then put 'em on your head

17:28.975 --> 17:31.642
to be a clown
from an Italian opera.

17:31.677 --> 17:34.712
♪ Laughing outside,
crying down below ♪

17:34.747 --> 17:37.381
♪ Pasta, meatballs,
Joe DiMaggio ♪

17:37.417 --> 17:41.385
♪ Fellatio, Pinocchio,
a pizza pie from Domino's ♪

17:41.421 --> 17:44.722
♪ All of this because
I'm singing in a pointy hat. ♪

17:44.757 --> 17:47.725
Look, Mr. Griffin's not here,
but if you leave your name,

17:47.760 --> 17:49.827
I'll let him know
you stopped by.

17:49.862 --> 17:51.896
Fine. Glenn Quagmire.

17:51.931 --> 17:53.798
Have him call me
the minute he gets in.

17:56.469 --> 17:58.469
They're gone.

17:59.472 --> 18:01.305
Well, for the next 72 hours,

18:01.340 --> 18:04.442
I'm gonna be harder to find
than a nice cat.

18:04.477 --> 18:06.977
You need me to clean out
your litter box?

18:10.650 --> 18:13.017
Mittens.

18:16.289 --> 18:18.456
Okay, Rupert, we're
going to play a game.

18:18.491 --> 18:20.090
I'm gonna be Buffalo Bill,

18:20.126 --> 18:22.393
and you're gonna be
a great big fat person.

18:23.663 --> 18:24.829
Close the lid.

18:24.864 --> 18:26.063
Brian? What are you doing?

18:26.098 --> 18:28.165
I'm hiding from Quagmire
for a few more hours.

18:28.201 --> 18:30.034
After that, he won't be able
to pull out of that deal.

18:30.069 --> 18:32.703
Well, if anybody knows how
to pull out, it's Quagmire.

18:35.608 --> 18:38.309
I have a lot of fun
up here in my room.

18:52.725 --> 18:55.159
Welcome home.

18:55.194 --> 18:57.161
Aah! Hey-Hey,
there, buddy.

18:57.196 --> 18:59.830
There you are. I've been
looking all over for you.

18:59.866 --> 19:01.999
That's why you've been
hiding from me in this motel?

19:02.034 --> 19:04.168
Now let me out of this deal
and give me my money back.

19:04.203 --> 19:06.537
Look, i-if you're not happy
with your current property,

19:06.572 --> 19:08.072
we could roll
your money over

19:08.107 --> 19:10.140
into something in
Sinkhole Estates.

19:10.176 --> 19:11.942
Those places are going
very fast, though.

19:11.978 --> 19:13.344
Who's a pilot you hate?

19:13.379 --> 19:14.945
You are such a scumbag.

19:14.981 --> 19:16.046
You know, when you were poor,

19:16.082 --> 19:17.248
you were always a douche,

19:17.283 --> 19:18.916
but at least you
came by it honestly.

19:18.951 --> 19:21.519
But now, screwing over
the people who helped you?

19:21.554 --> 19:24.021
I don't know how
you sleep at night.

19:25.925 --> 19:27.324
My God.

19:27.360 --> 19:28.826
You're right.

19:28.861 --> 19:30.327
I'm a jerk.

19:30.363 --> 19:33.531
I'm a selfish
and pretentious jerk.

19:33.566 --> 19:34.999
And you're
the only guy in town

19:35.034 --> 19:37.768
who's ever called me out
on my crap.

19:37.803 --> 19:39.870
You know, I used to hate you
for it, but...

19:39.906 --> 19:41.338
now I think
you're the only person

19:41.374 --> 19:43.407
who was trying
to be my friend.

19:43.442 --> 19:45.075
No, I think you're
misunderstanding me.

19:45.111 --> 19:46.277
No, I'm serious.

19:46.312 --> 19:48.045
Even though I know
you never liked me,

19:48.080 --> 19:50.381
you still helped me
when I really needed it.

19:50.416 --> 19:52.983
That says a lot
about your character.

19:53.019 --> 19:54.919
I'm ashamed of myself.

19:54.954 --> 19:57.288
Because I am none
of the things you are.

19:57.323 --> 20:00.257
You're honest, and direct,
and compassionate,

20:00.293 --> 20:01.892
and...

20:01.928 --> 20:03.260
that is 72 hours.

20:03.296 --> 20:05.529
Enjoy your craphole, dumbass.

20:05.565 --> 20:07.531
You son of a bitch!

20:13.172 --> 20:14.838
Wow, so I guess
that's it for you

20:14.874 --> 20:16.440
and real estate,
huh, Brian?

20:16.475 --> 20:19.009
Yeah, it was a lot
tougher than I thought.

20:19.045 --> 20:21.612
Oh, yeah, it's real hard
being a real estate agent.

20:21.647 --> 20:23.948
I mean, you got to be
able to count bathrooms.

20:23.983 --> 20:26.483
I once beat a real estate agent
in a game of chess.

20:26.519 --> 20:27.685
Me. A well-known buffoon.

20:27.720 --> 20:28.886
Face it,
you failed

20:28.921 --> 20:31.155
at people's
safety net job.

20:31.190 --> 20:33.023
Oh, come on, guys.
Give me a break, huh?

20:33.059 --> 20:34.358
I've had a
rough day.

20:34.393 --> 20:35.693
You've had
a rough day?

20:35.728 --> 20:37.837
You guys wouldn't
believe the day I've had.

20:37.837 --> 20:40.682
First of all, I didn't have any
clean underwear this morning,

20:40.683 --> 20:42.646
so I had to wear
a bathing suit.

20:42.647 --> 20:45.445
Then I missed the bus,
of course. Then it looked like

20:45.446 --> 20:47.286
it was gonna start to rain.
Luckily, it didn't.

20:47.998 --> 20:51.174
And like that wasn't enough,
then we had a pop quiz in history.

20:51.650 --> 20:54.175
Oh, European history. American
history was last year. Then...

20:54.176 --> 20:57.302
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru